e load helper function, but I wasn't sure how much this would cost -- I would basically activate/patch for every single file (so potentially many).\n\nAlso if we start using this internally the logging behavior must change: it is now taking on warning and info (the latter every single time).\n\nAny ideas @yarikoptic ?","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1508867692,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEzOlJlb3BlbmVkRXZlbnQxMzA4MzExNjA5"},"status":1},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1508876121,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMzOTExNzE4OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1884#issuecomment-339117189"},"message":"Overall I feel that using AutomagicIO for this might be slightly an overkill but hey -- it should have worked.  \nOk, situation is multifold\n- for AutomagicIO to work, underlying modules must not have those \"open\" etc methods pre-imported  in their spaces. So, instead of `from io import open`, use `import io; io.open`\n- it had no support for `io` or `lzma`\nI have quickly added those two into supported, but fighting some strange lzma.LZMAFile behavior... soon will submit a separate PR against masster, and will push into metadata branch","files":null}]}